      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "header",
          "bbox": [
            0.099,
            0.104,
            0.319,
            0.121
          ],
          "content": "ARITHMETIC PROGRESSIONS"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.873,
            0.105,
            0.899,
            0.119
          ],
          "content": "67"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.153,
            0.206,
            0.173
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.318,
            0.141,
            0.654,
            0.182
          ],
          "content": "S_{n}=\\frac{n\\left ( 1+n \\right ) }{2} \\quad \\mathrm{or} \\quad S_{n}=\\frac{n\\left ( n+1 \\right ) }{2}",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.193,
            0.627,
            0.213
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ **the sum of first n positive integers is given by**"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.422,
            0.227,
            0.57,
            0.268
          ],
          "content": "\\mathbf { S } _ { n } = { \\frac { n ( n + 1 ) } { 2 } }",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_5.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.279,
            0.902,
            0.318
          ],
          "content": "**Example 15 :** Find the sum of first 24 terms of the list of numbers whose nth term is given by"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.354,
            0.324,
            0.48,
            0.346
          ],
          "content": "a _ { _ n } = 3 + 2 n",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.349,
            0.205,
            0.367
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.375,
            0.135,
            0.393
          ],
          "content": "As"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.375,
            0.477,
            0.396
          ],
          "content": "a _ { _ n } = 3 + 2 n ,",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.403,
            0.133,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "so,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.35,
            0.399,
            0.497,
            0.421
          ],
          "content": "a _ { _ { 1 } } = 3 + 2 = 5",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.424,
            0.533,
            0.447
          ],
          "content": "a_{2}=3+2\\times 2=7",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_13.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.349,
            0.449,
            0.534,
            0.472
          ],
          "content": "a_{3} = 3 + 2 \\times 3 = 9",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_14.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.504,
            0.492,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "List of numbers becomes 5, 7, 9, 11, . . ."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.529,
            0.159,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "Here,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.322,
            0.529,
            0.679,
            0.548
          ],
          "content": "7-5=9-7=11-9=2  and so on.",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_17.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.554,
            0.579,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": "So, it forms an AP with common difference $d \\equiv 2.$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.578,
            0.535,
            0.599
          ],
          "content": "To find $S _ { 2 4 ^ { \\circ } }$ we have $n \\in 2 4 .$ , a = 5, d = 2."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.624,
            0.205,
            0.644
          ],
          "content": "Therefore,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.341,
            0.613,
            0.824,
            0.654
          ],
          "content": "S_{24} = \\frac{24}{2} \\left[ 2 \\times 5 + (24 - 1) \\times 2 \\right] = 12 \\left[ 10 + 46 \\right] = 672.",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_21.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.662,
            0.608,
            0.681
          ],
          "content": "$\\mathrm { S o } ,$ sum of first 24 terms of the list of numbers is 672."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.694,
            0.902,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": "**Example 16 :** A manufacturer of TV sets produced 600 sets in the third year and 700 sets in the seventh year. Assuming that the production increases uniformly by a fixed number every year, find :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.758,
            0.435,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "(i) the production in the 1st year"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.552,
            0.758,
            0.882,
            0.778
          ],
          "content": "(ii) the production in the 10th year"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.783,
            0.481,
            0.803
          ],
          "content": "(iii) the total production in first 7 years"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.095,
            0.808,
            0.9,
            0.848
          ],
          "content": "**Solution :** (i) Since the production increases uniformly by a fixed number every year, the number of TV sets manufactured in 1st, 2nd, 3rd, . . ., years will form an AP."
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.435,
            0.966,
            0.564,
            0.983
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.096,
            0.854,
            0.794,
            0.874
          ],
          "content": "Let us denote the number of TV sets manufactured in the nth year by $a _ { n ^ { * } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.879,
            0.159,
            0.898
          ],
          "content": "Then,"
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "bbox": [
            0.272,
            0.878,
            0.501,
            0.901
          ],
          "content": "a_{3}=600\\  and \\ a_{7}=700",
          "image_source": "images/page_18_equation_31.jpg"
        }
      ]
    }
